//! Peer wire protocol message types and error handling.
//!
//! This module implements the BitTorrent peer wire protocol as specified in
//! BEP 3. The wire protocol is used for all communication between peers after
//! initial discovery via the tracker.
//!
//! # Protocol Overview
//!
//! After TCP connection, peers exchange:
//! 1. A 68-byte handshake (not length-prefixed, unlike other messages)
//! 2. Length-prefixed messages for state and data exchange
//!
//! # Message Types
//!
//! | ID | Name | Payload |
//! |----|------|---------|
//! | - | keep-alive | (length = 0, no ID) |
//! | 0 | choke | none |
//! | 1 | unchoke | none |
//! | 2 | interested | none |
//! | 3 | not interested | none |
//! | 4 | have | piece index (4 bytes) |
//! | 5 | bitfield | bitfield |
//! | 6 | request | index, begin, length (12 bytes) |
//! | 7 | piece | index, begin, block |
//! | 8 | cancel | index, begin, length (12 bytes) |
//!
//! # Error Handling
//!
//! Peer communication can fail in many ways. The [`PeerError`] enum captures
//! all failure modes with appropriate detail for debugging and recovery.

